h card → 08_Checkout_Card, Pay on delivery → 09_Order_Complete\n8. **08_Checkout_Card**: close, Complete Order, \"Card Holder's Name\" Tony Chris, \"Card Number\" 1234 5678 9012 1314, \"Date\" 10/30, \"CVV\" 123, all filled, opens over 06_Basket. Links: close → 06_Basket, Complete Order → 09_Order_Complete\n9. **09_Order_Complete**: Track order, Continue shopping, \"Congratulations!!!\", \"Your order has been taken and is being attended to\", success mark (Icon_Success_Check). Links: Track order → 10_Track_Order, Continue shopping → 04_Home\n10. **10_Track_Order**: Go back, call the delivery agent, \"Delivery Status\", Map_Delivery, Steps: Order Taken (done, Step_Order_Taken), Order Is Being Prepared (done, Step_Order_Prepared), Order Is Being Delivered (current, \"Your delivery agent is coming\", Step_Order_Delivering), Order Received (not yet). Links: Go back → 04_Home\n\nFixed: primary color #FFA451 + Nunito font. Media from 04 · Media.\n\nNow let me read 01 · Foundations and 02 · Components and 04 · Media. I need to get design context (not just metadata) for accurate details. Let me get metadata first for those pages, then get design context on specific nodes as needed.\n\nThe reminder says I MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design. Let me do that for the reference pages. Let me first get metadata of pages 1:2 (Foundations), 1:3 (Components), 1:4 (Media), and 5:2 (Workspace) in parallel.","signature":"82ef0625f95c42e3920917a7"}],"id":"549295f9-3fdf-470e-afee-9dace6543c83","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dda6b51-cf28-47fc-8f32-0dff4e440494","uuid":"e211b1ad-9b69-4f65-b351-a985640130fc","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:04:45.411Z","thinking_duration_ms":12522}
