st get design context for the Button and Text Field symbols and status bar/home indicator. Actually, let me use use_figma read-only code to inspect them programmatically — that might be more token-efficient and give precise values. But the instructions say to use get_design_context. The reminder says \"After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design\". Let me call get_design_context on the key symbols (3:25, 3:28, 3:32, 3:42) and a couple of media symbols to understand their internal structure.\n\nActually, for cloning purposes I don't strictly need the internal details — `clone()` copies everything. But I need to know:\n- Fonts used in Button/Text Field text (I need to load them before editing text)\n- Colors of Button (probably #FFA451 background)\n- How the Status Bar / Home Indicator look (white/black content)\n\nLet me get design context for 3:25 (Button), 3:28 (Text Field), 3:32 (Status Bar), 3:42 (Home Indicator) in parallel.","signature":"3c3d4bb19bd44b749fe2f852"}],"id":"edaa4171-54ec-41ef-a1d7-cf47fe1467ac","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dda6b51-cf28-47fc-8f32-0dff4e440494","uuid":"530c28ee-a51e-4a96-aff1-f88701368913","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:05:19.767Z","thinking_duration_ms":13879}
