one lands on same page/parent; then `ws.appendChild(clone)` moves it. For COMPONENT clone → stays COMPONENT. \n\nFor status bar light: clone component → set children fills white: the text \"9:41\" fills white; Signal rects white; Wifi ellipse white; Battery stroke white + inner rect white; and component bg fill: transparent (none) — the master has white bg fill; for splash the bg behind is orange, so set clone fills = [] (transparent). Name \"FH / Status Bar · Light\". Home indicator light: bg transparent, bar white.\n\nSecondary button: clone button component, set fills white, strokes PRIMARY 1.5, text fill PRIMARY. Name \"FH / Button · Secondary\".\n\nField filled: clone Text Field, bg SOFT, text ink \"Value\". Hmm the filled fields in sheets have label+value stacked — make separate component \"FH / Field · Filled\": frame h=60 r10 bg #F8F5F0: label text 11 MUTED at (16,9); value text 14 SemiBold ink at (16,26). Master label \"Label\", value \"Value\".\n\nIcons: create instance helpers: `function icon(id, parent, x, y, w, h, color)` → instance, resize, recolor all vector children fills & strokes. Recoloring: walk instance children; for TEXT skip; set fills where fills length; strokes where strokes length. For Icon_Back (vector with stroke?) — it has 1 kid, probably a vector stroke. Set both fills and strokes.\n\nHeart recolor for \"selected\": white.\n\nLet me now also decide component master placement: components section frame \"🧩 Components\" at (0,0) size ~2000×800 with grid of masters. Masters inside a frame — allowed. But careful: components on page used by prototypes fine.\n\nActually simpler: place masters loose on page at negative coordinates (x from 0, y = -600 area)? Frames row at y≥0. Hmm, workspace cleanliness: put masters in a section frame at top: frame at (0, 0) w=2200 h=520, semi-transparent bg? Use fill #F8F7FB? Actually make it a normal frame named \"FH Design System\" with title text. Masters at grid positions inside.\n\nFrames layout (page coor