{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ALL 10 screen nodes are NULL. They don't exist in the document anymore!\n\nBut get_screenshot returned images for 12:57, 13:130, 13:182, 14:185, 17:275 just minutes ago! How?\n\nWait... maybe the screenshot tool cached them? Or... hmm. OR — maybe the screenshots I just took were served from a cache/CDN of earlier renders? The URLs are figma.com/api/mcp/asset/... — those could be cached renders from previous screenshot calls (in the earlier session I took screenshots of these same node IDs). The images returned match what the screens looked like AFTER the icon fixes though (icons look correct now — hamburger, chevron, check badges aligned). Hmm, actually wait — in round-1 screenshots (per summary), 04 had icon blocks and 10 had back/call/badge blocks. The screenshots I just got show FIXED versions. So they're NOT the old cached round-1 images... unless the fixes were verified by these screenshots when they were taken... \n\nHmm wait, actually. Let me think about what happened. Timeline per summary:\n1. Built all screens.\n2. Wired prototype.\n3. Screenshot round 1 → found icon issues.\n4. Ran icon fix script → ok.\n5. Splash logo fix → cleared.\n6. Session ended (compaction).\n7. Now: screenshots show FIXED state.\n8. But now nodes are NULL.\n\nIf nodes are NULL now, when did they disappear? Possibilities:\n- A rollback happened that removed everything? But \"failed scripts roll back entirely\" — the last successful ops were the paintIcon fix and logo fix. Those succeeded.\n- OR: the file was RESET between sessions? But the components 8:14-8:19, 9:13-9:43, 7:2 remain! And the screenshots showed the fixed state!\n\nWait, actually — are the components 8:14 etc. the ORIGINAL ones I created? They have the FH/ names I created. And 9:43 Step Row etc. inside 7:2. So the design system survived. But the screens are gone.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me re-check: maybe there's ANOTHER branch of the file? get_screenshot might have rendered from a branch? No — same fileKey.\n\nOR: maybe the document was modified between my screenshot calls and now? The screenshots at the start of this session showed the fixed icons — meaning at that time the nodes existed WITH fixes. Then something deleted them between then and now?!\n\nThat's really weird. Unless... the screenshot URLs returned were actually cached by the MCP server from the END of the previous session — i.e., the previous session took screenshots after fixes? Per the summary, \"The screens have NOT yet been re-screenshot after these fixes.\" Hmm.\n\nBut the images show fixes applied (e.g., 04's menu hamburger is visible, 10's back chevron visible, check badges green circles with white checks, call icon visible). Round-1 screenshots showed blocks. So these images must come from renders made AFTER the fix script ran. Who rendered them? The get_screenshot calls I just made — the MCP server renders on demand... but nodes are NULL now...\n\nUnless the rendering happened server-side before deletion? No — the deletion would have happened in the previous session, before these renders.\n\nWait wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe the screens exist on a DIFFERENT page that's NOT in figma.root.children?? Impossible — all pages are children of root.\n\nHmm, OR: the IDs 10:24 etc. might be from a stale session context where node IDs got renumbered after some operation. Figma IDs are stable though. When a script fails and rolls back, IDs don't persist. But successful ops keep IDs.\n\nActually — here's a thought: maybe between the fix script and now, the file was affected by version history restore, or the benchmark environment reset the file to a snapshot that included... no wait, if reset to pre-work state, the FH components wouldn't exist either.\n\nHmm, hold on — actually, let me look at what DOES exist: 7:2 frame with all FH components (7:5 Button Primary, 7:7 Secondary, 7:9 Text Field, 7:14/7:24 Status Bars, 7:34/7:36 Home Indicators, 8:14-8