heck: does `figma.root` have children that include the screens under some nested page? I listed all 5 pages with their direct children. Screens absent.\n\nAlso curious: the get_screenshot calls returned POST-FIX renders. If the nodes were already deleted BEFORE this session started, then the renders must have come from a cache created at the end of the previous session — meaning the MCP server had rendered them at some point post-fix... Per the summary, no screenshots were taken post-fix. But maybe the MCP server pre-renders? Or the previous session's summary was written slightly before the actual last actions (the \"messages after this summary kept verbatim\" note says the summary was written without seeing the most recent messages — maybe those messages included post-fix screenshots!). YES — the note says: \"The messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim.\" but I don't see them in my context... Actually the instruction said they'd be included but they seem absent. Regardless — plausibly the previous session DID take post-fix screenshots (which would be these images) and then... the screens still shouldn't disappear.\n\nHmm OK, actually — one very real possibility: THE FILE IS SHARED/BENCHMARK-MANAGED and got restored between sessions. Whatever the cause, I must rebuild the screens in the workspace page 5:2.\n\nWait, actually, let me do one more sanity check before the massive rebuild: search the entire document for any frames of size 375x812.","signature":"b72e563f9dae4e298cce41d5"}],"id":"27477494-c817-4134-a845-160cd960e64e","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2dda6b51-cf28-47fc-8f32-0dff4e440494","uuid":"f36c2480-ac4b-42bc-baf6-59ac05da6cc3","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:40:01.096Z","thinking_duration_ms":54632}
