{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_48fad6860b9a4d099d3711d8","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== BRIEF TEXTS ===\ny=64 sz=13 'LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2'\ny=96 sz=36 'Fruit Hub — fruit salad ordering app'\ny=162 sz=17 'Design the complete Fruit Hub mobile app: Tony tells the app their first name, browses fruit salad combos, adds one to the basket, checks out with delivery details or a card, and tracks the delivery. / Canvas 375 × 812, iPhone, light mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.'\ny=288 sz=24 'How to work'\ny=340 sz=15 '1. Build exactly the 10 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. / 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in screen order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. / 3. The brand primary color and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself (neutrals, text, surfaces, success / error / warning / disabled, supporting colors), plus type scale, spacing, radii and elevation, and apply them consistently. / 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button, a default Text Field and the platform shell (status bar, home indicator). Design all other states, the headers, the sheets and every business component as reusable components in your file. / 5. Use the logo, product photos, illustrations, map and icons from 04 · Media. Prices use the Naira glyph (Icon_Naira or “₦”). / 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.'\ny=595 sz=24 'Frames · goals · must include · links'\ny=647 sz=15 'Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.'\ny=711 s