o!)\n- Berry_Mango 2:17: b585f5...\n- Quinoa 2:20: f3964b... (matches Card·Combo S + Row·Basket default)\n- Tropical 2:23: c1bfb8...\n- Melon 2:26: 1965b0...\n- Basket_Welcome 2:32: edcf8e...\n- Basket_Name 2:35: 70de1d...\n- Fruit_Drops 2:38: c029d1...\n- Step_Taken 2:41: 6a31d1... (Step Row default illus)\n- Step_Prepared 2:44: 663f0e...\n- Step_Delivering 2:47: aba6d9...\n- Map 2:50: 1e1a48...\n\nMedia components have image fills directly on the component (IMG hash present on the component node itself). So to swap a card's photo: `cardInst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"photo\").fills = [imagePaintFromHash]`. I'll construct image paints: {type:\"IMAGE\", scaleMode:\"FILL\" or \"FIT\", imageHash}. Since I can't call createImageAsync (forbidden), I reuse existing imageHash strings — that works: setting fills with an imageHash that exists in the document is fine.\n\nWait — CAN I construct {type:\"IMAGE\", imageHash:\"...\", scaleMode:\"FILL\"} without figma.createImage? Yes, plugin API allows assigning paint objects with imageHash referencing existing images. The components themselves have those hashes so they're valid.\n\nAlso note: 2:8 Logo component has IMG fill directly. So for splash: instance of 2:8, resize 198x153, clear the instance container fills? Wait — if the component has the IMG fill directly on itself, clearing instance fills would remove the logo image! But per summary the previous fix \"cleared its fills\" of \"Logo_Fruit_Hub INSTANCE\" — hmm, that would erase the logo image...\n\nWait, let me reconsider. In the previous splash, the logo instance had a WHITE BOX behind the logo. If the IMG fill is on the component itself and the instance showed a white box, the white box must come from... a child of the component? The media map shows only IMG on 2:8 itself, no children listed (dump showed no child info lines for 2:8, meaning no children or no image children). If 2:8 has no children and direct IMG fill, then the white box in the splash screenshot was probably