eplaced). Then \"clearing\" restores image. That fits: white fill override → white box; cleared → image shows.\n\nWhy would the instance have a white fill override? Maybe I explicitly set it (mistakenly) in the build script to give the logo a background. Yes — likely I set white fills on the logo instance as a \"card bg\" mistake. Fix was correct.\n\nFor rebuild: instance of 2:8, resize 198x153, DON'T touch fills (inherits image fill). Done.\n\nSimilarly salad photos: instances inherit image fills. But scale: component 2:20 is 180x120 (ratio 1.5); card photo 87x87 square with scaleMode FIT. When I set fills override with hash, use scaleMode \"FILL\" for square containers? Card S photo default fill scaleMode FIT with hash f3964b (quinoa 180x120 into 87x87 FIT → letterboxed, image centered at 87x58?). Hmm — but the screenshot shows photos nicely filling. FIT within a white circle-ish container... In screenshot 04, quinoa photo appears as a round plate on white — fine with FIT (white bg of card). OK keep FIT.\n\nFor overrides I'll set: photoInst.fills = [{type:\"IMAGE\", scaleMode:\"FILL\", imageHash: HASH}] — FILL crops to fill square; screenshots from earlier looked good with FIT... Actually the previous build set specific paints via `inst.findOne(...).fills = figma.getNodeById(\"2:23\").fills` — copying the component's exact paint (FIT + hash). That produced the good screenshots. I'll do the same: copy fills from media components directly.\n\nTropical 2:23 hash c1bfb8, Melon 2:26 hash 1965b0, Honey 2:14 ee1682 (already default in M card), Berry 2:17 b585f5.\n\nRow·Basket rows: quinoa (default), melon (1965b0), tropical (c1bfb8).\n\nStep Row illus overrides: row2 663f0e (prepared), row3 aba6d9 (delivering), row4 hidden.\n\nNow — illustrations for 02/03: Basket_Welcome 2:32 (301x260), Basket_Name 2:35 (301x281), Fruit_Drops 2:38 (96x72) — used as decorative accents. 02 must include BOTH Basket_Welcome AND Fruit_Drops. 03 both Basket_Name AND Fruit_Drops. 09: success c