ontent true + cornerRadius 16); Step Rows x=22 y=347,429,511,593 (h80 each; ends 673).\n  Row overrides:\n  - r1: illus default (Step_Order_Taken hash already default 6a31d1), title \"Order Taken\", sub \"Your order has been received\"? Brief copy for r1 sub: from screenshot \"Your order has been received\". Brief fixed copy says only Order Taken ✓... screenshot showed \"Your order has been received\". Use it.\n  - r2: illus 663f0e, title \"Order Is Being Prepared\", sub \"Your salad is being prepared\".\n  - r3: illus aba6d9, title \"Order Is Being Delivered\" color PRIMARY, sub \"Your delivery agent is coming\", iconDone hidden, overlay ellipse 14x14 PRIMARY at (82, 525).\n  - r4: illus visible=false, title \"Order Received\" color MUTED, sub \"Enjoy your fruit salad\", iconDone hidden, overlay ellipse white + stroke #D9D6E0 1.5 at (82, 607).\n  Connector rects 2x38: (88, 383) PRIMARY, (88, 465) PRIMARY, (88, 547) #D9D6E0.\n  Wait — check alignment: badges at component iconDone @ (58,12) size 18 → global x=22+58=80, y=row+12. Center x=89. Lines x=88 w=2 → center 89 ✓. Row1 y=347: badge y=359-377. Line1 y=383: gap 6 below badge1, h=38 → ends 421; row2 badge y=429+12=441-459: gap 20. Hmm uneven. Previously lines at y=383/465/547 h38 — screenshot showed lines connecting badges decently. Keep same.\n  - Prototype: back→04.\n\nBuild plan (scripts):\n- Script B: 01_Splash + 02_Welcome + 03_Name.\n- Script C: 04_Home.\n- Script D: 05_Product_Quinoa.\n- Script E: 06_Basket.\n- Script F: 07 + 08 (clone-ish, built fresh).\n- Script G: 09 + 10.\n- Script H: prototype wiring (needs final IDs).\n- Screenshots + fixes.\n\nCommon helper block (define once per script):\n```js\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(figma.getNodeById(\"5:2\"));\nawait Promise.all([\n  figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Nunito\",style:\"Regular\"}),\n  figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Nunito\",style:\"SemiBold\"}),\n  figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Nunito\",style:\"Bold\"})\n]);\nconst P=(hex,o)=>{const n=parseInt(hex,16);return{type:\"SOLID\",color:{r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255},opacity:o===undefined?1:o};};\nconst PRIMARY=\"FFA451\", INK=\"27214D\", BODY=\"6C6980\", MUTED=\"A8A3BC\", FAINT=\"C2BDBD\", SOFT=\"F8F5F0\", TINT=\"FFF1E3\", LINE=\"F0EDF3\", GRAY=\"D9D6E0\", WHITE=\"FFFFFF\";\nfunction frame(name,x,y){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;f.resize(375,812);f.x=x;f.y=y;f.fills=[P(WHITE)];f.clipsContent=true;figma.currentPage.appendChild(f);return f;}\nfunction txt(parent,str,size,style,hex,x,y,w,lh){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:\"Nunito\",style:style};t.characters=str;t.fontSize=size;t.fills=[P(hex)];if(w)t.resize(w,t.height);if(lh)t.lineHeight={unit:\"PERCENT\",value:lh};parent.appendChild(t);t.x=x;t.y=y;return t;}\nfunction inst(id,parent,x,y){const i=figma.getNodeById(id).createInstance();parent.appendChild(i);i.x=x;i.y=y;return i;}\nfunction recolor(i,hex){const kids=i.children||[];for(const c of kids){if(Array.isArray(c.fills)&&c.fills.length&&c.fills!==figma.mixed)c.fills=[P(hex)];if(Array.isArray(c.strokes)&&c.strokes.length)c.strokes=[P(hex)];}}\n```\nNote: recolor for icons — icon components have container fills white; instance container fills must be cleared first: `i.fills=[]` then recolor children. For icons 2:59/2:65/2:73/2:78/2:94/2:134 — check whether they have bg children. From summary: Menu 2:59 vectors #070648 (container white); Search 2:65 #86869e; Filter 2:73 stroke vectors; Heart 2:78 stroke #ffa451; Basket 2:94 vector #ffa451; Call 2:134 (2 vectors #070648). Add 2:89 and Plus 2:112 have bg circle. Minus 2:106 strokes. So for menu/search/filter/heart/basket/call: i.fills=[] then paint children with target color. For heart: strokes matter (stroke vector).\n\nHmm wait — do I know 2:94 (Basket) has white container? Summary: \"Basket 2:94 (vector #ffa451)\" — listed container fills white presumably like others (\"every icon COMPONENT (2:59–2:140) has a container frame with fills:#ffffff\"). So clear insta