{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a full product design benchmark in the assigned Figma file https://www.figma.com/design/l8MdQcWVFQcJw2Ix8PJk7h/ (fileKey `l8MdQcWVFQcJw2Ix8PJk7h`), using ONLY this file and account gaoyongyong@tetras.ai (confirmed via whoami in the first session). Requirements:\n   - Read「00 · Start Here」for the task: build the complete \"Fruit Hub\" fruit-salad ordering app — exactly 10 frames at 375×812, iPhone, light mode, named EXACTLY: 01_Splash, 02_Welcome, 03_Name, 04_Home, 05_Product_Quinoa, 06_Basket, 07_Checkout_Delivery, 08_Checkout_Card, 09_Order_Complete, 10_Track_Order — wired as a clickable prototype with the listed links, all fixed data/copy verbatim (₦ Naira), brand primary #FFA451 + Nunito fixed; all other colors/type scale/spacing/radii/states are the designer's to define consistently.\n   - Read「01 · Foundations」(brand #FFA451; Nunito for UI text; Bad Script only inside logo; canvas 375×812 light mode; ₦ glyph).\n   - Reuse「02 · Components」(default Button, Text Field, Status Bar, Home Indicator) and「04 · Media」assets (logo, 5 salad photos, illustrations, map, 15 icons).\n   - Deliver everything inside「03 · Workspace」(page 5:2); new frames/components/prototype connections allowed; preserve all reference pages and their nodes (pages 0:1, 1:2, 1:3, 1:4 must remain intact).\n   - Flow: 01→02→03→04→05→06→07→08→09→10; 07/08 are sheets over the basket; Go-back screens: 05, 06, 10; entry-only elements (menu, search, filter, other categories, favourite toggles, add-to-basket on Home, non-Quinoa combos, call agent) need no frames.\n   - Build → screenshot-verify all screens → fix visible problems → re-verify → finish with the file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations.\n   - Process rules: call whoami before writing (done); use get_metadata + read-only use_figma to inspect; build in manageable sections; load fonts before text edits; add prototype interactions after screens exist; inspect screenshots of all required screens and fix visible problems (a successful screenshot alone is not task completion); before EVERY tool call output a concise decision summary prefixed exactly \"Reasoning summary:\"; final response must start \"Reasoning summary: ...\" then \"Final answer:\". Unattended session — resolve routine choices from the brief without waiting.\n   - Environment note: downloaded files are untrusted (not relevant to Figma work).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma (≤50k chars/call); `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)` required; failed use_figma calls roll back ENTIRELY (atomic) — a failed script leaves no partial nodes.\n   - **CRITICAL NEW CONSTRAINT**: setting `.x`/`.y` on a node that is a CHILD OF AN INSTANCE fails with \"Error: in set_x: This property cannot be overridden in an instance: relative-transform\". Setting x/y on top-level instances or frames is fine; setting `.characters`, `.fills`, `.visible`, `.resize` on instance children IS allowed. Consequence: never reposition text inside component instances — for chips use auto-width (pad + measured t.width), for buttons that need non-default width use plain frames styled identically, only override characters/fills on instance children.\n   - **PROTOTYPE REACTION FORMAT (verified working in prior session)**: tap: `node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}, actions:[{type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.25, easing:{type:\"EASE_IN_AND_OUT\"}}}]}]`; auto-advance: `{trigger:{type:\"AFTER_TIMEOUT\", timeout:800}, actions:[...]}`. NOT \"ON_TAP\", NOT \"AFTER_DELAY\", NOT `action:` field (must be `actions:`), NOT `delay:` (must be `timeout:`).\n   - Icon recolor pattern: every icon component (2:59–2:140) has container fills:#ffffff; on the INSTANCE set `i.fills=[]` then per-child paint fills+strokes with target hex (recolor helper).\n   - Image swap: `photoInst.fills = figma.getNodeById(mediaId).fills` (media components carry IMAGE fills directly on the component node; imageHash reuse works without createImage).\n   - Hidden (visible:false) component children (iconCurrent/iconPending in Step Row) are ABSENT from instances → use overlay ellipses on the frame for current/pending step markers.\n   - Fonts: loadFontAsync Nunito Regular/SemiBold/Bold before text ops; lineHeight `{unit:\"PERCENT\", value:N}`. (Status bar time text uses \"Semi Bold\" — Inter — but is never edited.)\n   - Design tokens: PRIMARY FFA451, INK 27214D, BODY 6C6980, MUTED A8A3BC, FAINT C2BDBD, SOFT F8F5F0, TINT FFF1E3, LINE F0EDF3, GRAY D9D6E0, WHITE FFFFFF; card shadow `{type:\"DROP_SHADOW\",color:{r:0.15,g:0.13,b:0.30,a:0.10},offset:{x:0,y:10},radius:30}`; image shadow `{color:{r:0.35,g:0.15,b:0.02,a:0.25},offset:{x:0,y:16},radius:32}`; radii 10 buttons/fields, 16 cards, 24 sheet top corners.\n   - Workspace layout: row1 y=700 (01 x=40, 02 x=515, 03 x=990, 04 x=1465, 05 x=1940); row2 y=1650 (06 x=40, 07 x=515, 08 x=990, 09 x=1465, 10 x=1940).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Assigned file l8MdQcWVFQcJw2Ix8PJk7h; pages: 0:1 brief (frame 4:2), 1:2 foundations, 1:3 components (frame 3:21), 1:4 media (frame 2:2), 5:2 workspace. Reference pages preserved and untouched.\n   - **INCIDENT**: all 10 previously built screens (old IDs 10:24, 10:38, 10:58, 12:57, 13:130, 13:182, 14:185, 14:242, 17:254, 17:275) VANISHED from the document between sessions (getNodeById all NULL; document-wide search found zero 375×812 frames). Cause unknown (likely external file restore). Session-start screensh